PART 2: UNDERSTANDING THE useState HOOK
================================================================================

WHAT IS THE useState HOOK?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The useState hook is:

• A React Hook
  - Imported from the React library

• A State Management Tool
  - Adds local state to a functional component

• Returns Two Values
  - Current state value
  - State setter function

• Enables Re-rendering
  - State setter calls can cause React to render with updated state

• Used with Immutable Patterns
  - Objects and arrays should be replaced rather than mutated

• Used in Function Components
  - Common mechanism for component-local state

• Simple API
  - Easy to understand for basic state requirements

• Foundation for Interactivity
  - Supports dynamic and interactive UI behavior


================================================================================
useState HOOK SYNTAX
================================================================================

Basic syntax:

const [state, setState] = useState(initialValue)


BREAKDOWN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+-------------------+--------------------------------------------------+
| PART              | MEANING                                          |
+-------------------+--------------------------------------------------+
| const             | Declares the state/setter bindings               |
| state             | Current state value                              |
| setState          | Function used to request a state update          |
| useState()        | React Hook for component-local state             |
| initialValue      | Initial state value                              |
| Return            | [currentValue, setterFunction]                   |
+-------------------+--------------------------------------------------+


EXAMPLE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const [count, setCount] = useState(0)


Meaning:

count
  ↓
Current State Value


setCount
  ↓
Function Used to Update State


0
  ↓
Initial Value


================================================================================
WRONG WAY VS useState WAY
================================================================================

+----------------------+-------------------------+---------------------------+
| ASPECT               | WRONG WAY               | useState WAY              |
+----------------------+-------------------------+---------------------------+
| Creating state       | let count = 0           | useState(0)               |
| Updating state       | count = count + 1       | setCount(count + 1)       |
| React state update   | No                      | Yes                       |
| UI update            | Not state-driven        | State-driven              |
| Mutation risk        | High                    | Avoid with proper updates |
| Debugging            | Harder                  | More predictable          |
| Component behavior   | Unreliable              | Predictable               |
| React pattern        | Incorrect for state     | Standard local-state Hook |
+----------------------+-------------------------+---------------------------+


