PART 6: useState WITH DIFFERENT DATA TYPES
================================================================================

useState works with different JavaScript data types.


1. STRING STATE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const [name, setName] = useState('John')

setName('Jane')


2. NUMBER STATE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const [count, setCount] = useState(0)

setCount(count + 1)


3. BOOLEAN STATE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false)

setIsOpen(!isOpen)


Recommended when based on previous value:

setIsOpen(previous =>
  !previous
)


4. ARRAY STATE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const [items, setItems] = useState([])

setItems([
  ...items,
  newItem
])


5. OBJECT STATE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const [user, setUser] = useState({
  name: '',
  age: 0
})


setUser({
  ...user,
  name: 'John'
})


6. NESTED OBJECT STATE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const [data, setData] = useState({

  user: {
    name: '',
    age: 0
  },

  settings: {
    theme: 'light'
  }

})


setData({

  ...data,

  user: {
    ...data.user,
    name: 'John'
  }

})


DATA TYPE COMPARISON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+------------------+-------------------------+----------------------------------+
| DATA TYPE        | INITIAL VALUE           | UPDATE PATTERN                   |
+------------------+-------------------------+----------------------------------+
| String           | useState('text')        | setState('new text')             |
| Number           | useState(0)             | setState(value + 1)              |
| Boolean          | useState(false)         | setState(!value)                 |
| Array            | useState([])            | setState([...arr, item])         |
| Object           | useState({})            | setState({...obj, prop: value})  |
| Nested Object    | useState({a:{b:0}})     | Copy each changed level          |
| Array of Objects | useState([{id:1}])      | setState(arr.map(...))           |
| Mixed Object     | useState({arr:[],       | Copy object + changed property   |
|                  | count:0})               |                                  |
+------------------+-------------------------+----------------------------------+


