CRITICAL POINTS TO REMEMBER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Use useState for local information that must persist across renders
  and affect rendering

• Use the returned setter to update state

• Treat objects and arrays in state as read-only

• Create updated objects/arrays instead of mutating existing ones

• Use spread syntax where appropriate

• Use map() to update array items immutably

• Use filter() to remove array items immutably

• Use functional setters when the next value depends on previous state

• Provide meaningful initial values

• Keep state minimal

• Don't duplicate values that can be calculated from existing state/props

• Use stable keys when rendering lists


